# 3. Datasets

We directly use the processed datasets released by the BCIPM work.
The datasets include: Tmall、Taobao、Yelp.
• Taobao: An e-commerce dataset under the Alibaba Group containing behaviors click, cart, and purchase. We treat purchase as the target behavior, while click and cart serve as auxiliary behaviors. 
• Tmall: Another widely-used e-commerce dataset from Alibaba with behaviors click,collect,cart,andpurchase. The target behavior is designated as purchase. 
• Yelp: A business review dataset comprising tips and ratings. Ratings r are discretized into dislike(r≤2),neutral (2<r<4),and like(r≥4). The like behavior is treated as the target, with others acting as auxiliary signals.
The data format follows the same structure used in prior multi-behavior recommendation studies.

# 4. Data Split

We follow the evaluation protocol used in BCIPM.
Specifically, the datasets are pre-split using the leave-one-out strategy.
For each user:
• the most recent interaction is used for testing
• the second most recent interaction is used for validation
• the remaining interactions are used for training
This protocol is widely adopted in recommendation research.

# 5. Evaluation Metrics

We adopt full-ranking evaluation.
For each test user, the model ranks all candidate items that do not appear in the user's training interactions.
Evaluation metrics:
• HR@K (Hit Ratio)
• NDCG@K (Normalized Discounted Cumulative Gain)
We evaluate the model at: K ∈ {10, 20, 50, 80}. The paper mainly reports HR@10 and NDCG@10.

# 6. Training Settings

Unless otherwise specified, the following training settings are used.
| Parameter | Value |
|----------|------|
Embedding dimension | {64, 128} |
Batch size | 1024 |
Optimizer | Adam |
GCN propagation layers | 2 |
The model is trained with a joint objective consisting of:
• Target ranking loss (BPR)
• Behavior-level discrimination loss
• Target propensity loss
• L2 regularization
During training, random negative sampling is adopted:
• 8 negative samples per positive instance for the behavior BCE loss and target propensity loss
• 1 negative item per positive interaction for the target BPR ranking loss
Model selection is based on NDCG@10 on the validation set. Results reported in the paper are averaged over 5 runs with different random seeds. Early stopping is applied if validation NDCG@10 does not improve for 10 consecutive epochs.
All experiments are implemented in PyTorch and executed on a Linux server with an NVIDIA GPU (~12GB memory).

# 7. Hyperparameter Search

Hyperparameters are tuned using grid search on the validation set.
Search ranges:
Learning rate 
  - [1e-4, 1e-3, 1e-2]
Loss weighting coefficients
  - λ₁ ∈ [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]
  - λ₂ ∈ [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]
Regularization coefficient
  - µ ∈ [1e-4, 1e-3, 1e-2]
The best configuration is selected according to NDCG@10 on the validation set.

# 8. Baseline Models

For fair comparison:
• All baseline models follow the same dataset split and evaluation protocol.
• Baseline implementations follow the settings described in their original papers.
• Hyperparameters are tuned on the validation set when necessary.
The tuning ranges follow commonly used values reported in the recommendation literature.

# 9. Training

Run training with default settings:
 python main.py
Run training on specific datasets:
 python main.py --data_name tmall
 python main.py --data_name yelp
 python main.py --data_name taobao

